# Trivy ignore list (image scans).
# Each entry MUST include: severity, justification, expiry-or-followup.
# Re-evaluate every time we bump caddy / dependencies.
#
# How to re-audit (no docker needed): read the dependency versions caddy pins
# in its own go.mod for the tag we build —
#   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/caddyserver/caddy/<CADDY_VERSION>/go.mod
# — then ask OSV whether that exact version is still affected:
#   POST https://api.osv.dev/v1/query {"package":{"name":"<mod>","ecosystem":"Go"},"version":"<ver>"}
# An empty result means caddy has moved past the fix and the entry below is
# dead weight; delete it. OSV and trivy's DB are not identical, so confirm on
# the next CI run — the docker-images job scans with exit-code 0 and prints the
# full HIGH/CRITICAL table.
#
# Caddy v2.11.9 (2026-11-05) ships x/net v0.60.0 and go-jose v4.1.6, which
# cleared the x/net HTTP/2 entry (CVE-2026-78669) carried for v2.11.7. OSV
# still lists for v2.11.9, not reported by trivy:
#
#   * GO-2026-5932 (x/crypto/openpgp unmaintained) has no CVE/GHSA alias.
#   * GO-2026-6866 (x/net v0.60.0 html, fix 0.62.0) is MEDIUM. Its sibling
#     GO-2026-6860 is HIGH and has an entry below.
#   * GO-2026-6865 (klauspost/compress v1.20.1, fix 1.20.2): the zstd decoder
#     panics on a crafted frame. Caddy only encodes responses with zstd and
#     never decodes untrusted zstd input.
#   * GHSA-4w3g-jfj2-cw2q and GHSA-vvm8-gf78-28g4 (go-jose v3.0.5 panics) are
#     MODERATE, below the release gate.

# === caddy gobinary, frontend + panel images ==================================
#
# Caddy v2.11.9 pins go-jose v4.1.6 (fixed) and still pulls in v3.0.5 through
# smallstep. GHSA-mgcc-cww5-fp2q (2026-10-27) is a CPU DoS when parsing a JWK
# that holds an RSA key; v3 has no fix. Caddy reaches go-jose only through the
# smallstep CA code behind the `acme_server` handler and the `pki` app, which
# parse JWKs sent by ACME clients. Neither Caddyfile configures them and both
# set `auto_https off`, so no untrusted JWK is ever parsed.
#
# Followup: drop this entry once a caddy release no longer pulls in go-jose v3.

CVE-2026-116587       # HIGH go-jose v3.0.5 (no fix) — RSA JWK parse DoS; caddy has no acme_server or pki configured, never parses untrusted JWKs.

# Caddy v2.11.9 pins x/net v0.60.0. GO-2026-6860 (GHSA-75pg-wvh3-34jr, raised
# to HIGH on 2026-11-04) is quadratic time in the x/net/html parser when it
# coalesces many short text runs. Caddy core never imports x/net/html; it is
# linked only through smallstep/cli-utils/usage (CLI help rendering), and
# govulncheck on caddy v2.11.9 `cmd/caddy` reports no call path to Parse or
# ParseFragment. Our Caddyfiles only proxy and serve
# static files, so no request or response body is parsed as HTML.
#
# Followup: drop this entry once a caddy release ships x/net >= 0.62.0.

CVE-2026-78661        # HIGH x/net v0.60.0 html (fix 0.62.0) — parser quadratic text coalescing DoS; govulncheck finds no call path from cmd/caddy, caddy never parses HTML.
